{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 190,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When people talk about the physics of American\nfootball, they normally mention force, torque,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4570,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so on…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5570,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like how the energy from two linemen colliding\nis enough to power a 60W light bulb for over"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9900,
    "dDurationMs": 4559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a minute, or is equivalent to an average person\nfalling two stories off of a building!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14459,
    "dDurationMs": 4441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there's another aspect of physics in football\nthat isn't talked about as much – symmetry!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18900,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You might think symmetry is just for butterflies\nand rorschach tests, but it's all over the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22760,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "place in football: there's translational symmetry\nwhen teams keep the same formations as they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26900,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "move up or down the field, and rotational\nsymmetry when they switch sides after a touchdown."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31620,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even the ball has axial symmetry so it can\nspin smoothly through the air."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35910,
    "dDurationMs": 2989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why is symmetry useful in the first place?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38899,
    "dDurationMs": 4701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Symmetry makes things easier, or at least\nmore efficient; it gives you a guide: \"same"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43600,
    "dDurationMs": 1739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scenario, same action.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45339,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means you don't have to reinvent the\nwheel all the time: to draw a straight line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49079,
    "dDurationMs": 1561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you just keep drawing in the same direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50640,
    "dDurationMs": 3130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For a circle, keep curving the same amount."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53770,
    "dDurationMs": 3789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when football players practice a play over\nand over, the patterns of football become"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57559,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so ingrained in their reflexes they can act\nwithout thinking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61019,
    "dDurationMs": 5131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Psychologists call this \"habit formation\";\nwe call it \"symmetry in time\"!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66150,
    "dDurationMs": 3350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And when players line up on the field the\nsame way at the thirty, or forty, or fifty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69500,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yard lines, that's \"symmetry in space\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72400,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even physics itself is symmetric – ever\nheard of Newton's law: \"a body in motion tends"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76730,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to stay in motion\"?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78210,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's just nature saying \"keep doing the\nsame thing.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81070,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's more, Newton's laws of motion are the\nsame now as they were yesterday, and they'll"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85130,
    "dDurationMs": 1330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be the same again tomorrow!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86460,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Doesn't that make life easy?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88340,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultimately, symmetry is what allows both science\nAND football to function - if the laws of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92560,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the universe (or the rules of football) changed\nfrom day to day, we wouldn't be able to repeat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97060,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "experiments, make predictions, or know what\nplays to practice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100750,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when you reach for yet another handful\nof chips while watching the next football"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103710,
    "dDurationMs": 14230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "game, know that millions across the country\nare doing exactly the same, in perfect symmetry."
    } ]
  } ]
}
